


Argument Handling "args.h"

            The args.h header specifies a struct that is
            intended to facilitate argument handling.

            Objects of type args should be modified by the
            args_import function only.

        Functions

            The args_import function parses words from the
            short string specified by #1 and initializes the
            args object specified by #0 accordingly.

            The args_nmemb function returns the number of
            arguments represented by the args object
            specified by #0.

            The args_fetch function overwrites the array
            specified by #0 with the #2-th argument of the
            args object specified by #1.
